member.remarks:
Variable resolution: if  is a supported primitive (see ), every variable is replaced by the value itself;
if it's an array of a supported type or of , the variable is the element index (ex: "{0}") or an element name (see );
otherwise the variable names a public instance property or field.
Use "{{" to emit a literal '{'. Strings, floating point values and  values are url escaped.
Elements of an  array are formatted at runtime based on their type, like the typed values (invariant culture), other types (ex: enums) use ;
they are always url escaped and null becomes an empty string.
Compiled functions are cached per template (thread safe, a template may be compiled more than once under contention).
